To install the latest  stable "kubectl"  from the official kubernetes repository on the ubuntu "ec2"
____________________________________________________________________________________________________

>> sudo apt update
>> sudo apt install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificate curl 

ca-certificates: This installs a collection of trusted Certificate Authority (CA) certificates
These certificates allow your system to verify  that an HTTPS server's certificate is trustworthy

apt-transport-https: This package allowed apt to communicate with software repository using https (historicallY) 
not needed now

Add the kubernetes signing key: 
_______________________________

>> sudo mkdir -p -m 755 /etc/apt/keyrings
>> curl -fsSL https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.34/deb/Release.key | \
>> sudo gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.gpg


Add the repository: 
_________________________________

>> echo 'deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.gpg] https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.34/deb/ /' | \
sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list

Install the kubectl : 
_________________________________

>> sudo apt update
>> sudo apt install -y kubectl

Verify : 
_________________________________

>> kubectl version --client
